This small set of files is grouped for your convenience, as all you'll
need to cope with most ZIP files on your Psion computer.

Copy the UNZIP.HLP, UNZIP.IMG and the UNZIP.OPA (or UNZIP.CLS is you've got a
Series 3 'Classic') to the same \APP\ directory and install the icon with
Psion-I as usual. Then run and follow all prompts/dialogs etc.

Detailed instructions are contained within the UNZIP.TXT file.

Notes:
-----------------
1) Large ZIP files will require LOTS of free memory to extract
correctly, you have been warned.

2) For full details on the UNZIP.IMG program, I refer you to the
original S3UZ150L.ZIP archive, which contains David Palmer's original
release notes and details of all the wierd and wonderful command line
switches. This archive should be available from the same place you
obtained *this* file.

3) Siena owners can use either .OPA file. The 3a version has slightly too
wide a dialog but by judicious use of the TAB key you can get it all
working without problem. The Series 3 version fits the screen but uses a
very small font. It's up to you!
